# tests/gates/omega-kernel-crypto-boundary.gate
# Aienux, folded into kernel/ (Drake 2026-11-17, kernel/MIGRATION.md).
# Aienux AIENOS-CRYPTO-BOUNDARY, unchanged: kernel/tests/gates/run.sh crypto-boundary, reached from the
# omega-mv root as tests/gates/run.sh kernel-crypto-boundary. Inputs are aienux's, under kernel/. Its aienux manifest:
# Hosted: none (#427 removed the hosted test workflows; the Spark runs this locally). Formerly crypto-boundary.yml: cargo test/clippy of aienos-crypto, aienos-kernel crypto:: tests, no_std check of aienos-kernel (hosted 23 s; always-run)
gate: OMEGA-KERNEL-CRYPTO-BOUNDARY
manifest_version: 2
owner: omega
requires:
  - host
inputs:
  - kernel/crates/aienos-crypto/
  - kernel/crates/aienos-kernel/
  - kernel/Cargo.toml
  - kernel/Cargo.lock
  - kernel/vendor/
  - kernel/tests/gates/
  - kernel/crates/
  - kernel/.cargo/
  - kernel/docs/adr/0015-golden-vectors.json
  - tests/gates/omega-kernel-crypto-boundary.gate
  - tests/gates/run.sh
run:
  exec: tests/gates/run.sh
  args: ["kernel-crypto-boundary"]
expects:
  exit: 0
  verdict: PASS
timeout: 15m
exactness: EXACT
cache_scope: machine
